1. LiDAR fog simulation (fog_simulation.py, fog_lookup_tables/)
   Adapted from Martin Hahner et al., LiDAR fog simulation, https://github.com/MartinHahner/LiDAR_fog_sim
   (repository licence: CC BY-NC 4.0; the paper to cite is given in that repository's README).
   Upstream commit: UNRESOLVED.
   The fog lookup tables were obtained from MultiCorrupt's converter/fog_lookup_tables/ (see 3); they
   were generated by integration code derived from LiDAR_fog_sim and are treated as covered by
   CC BY-NC 4.0. They are shipped as .npz arrays holding the same values as the original pickle files;
   fog_lookup_tables/SOURCES.txt records the sha256 of the original files.

2. LiDAR snowfall simulation (snow_simulation.py, snowflake_sampling.py)
   Adapted from Martin Hahner et al.'s LiDAR snowfall simulation, published at CVPR 2022 ("LiDAR Snowfall
   Simulation"; the full citation is given in the upstream repository's README),
   https://github.com/SysCV/LiDAR_snow_sim (tools/snowfall/simulation.py, sampling.py; files state
   __license__ = "CC BY-NC 4.0"). Upstream commit: UNRESOLVED.
   snow_simulation.py as received via MultiCorrupt also carried two small helpers of unknown licence:
   ransac_polyfit (idea originally from https://gist.github.com/geohot/9743ad59598daf61155bf0d43a10838c) and
   binary_angle_search (originally from https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/python-program-for-binary-search).
   They are not included: the snow code calls MIT-licensed reimplementations written for CoopFaultBench from
   a description of what they compute (coopfaultbench/injectors/_snow_helpers.py), verified byte-identical.
   snow_laser.yaml (an HDL-64 sensor calibration) was obtained from MultiCorrupt's converter/; its
   deeper origin is UNRESOLVED; it is placed here because its only consumer is the snow simulation.

